Build: data model, stack and phases
Core tables. users (role, language, phone, status); devices (owner's approved devices); applicants; referrals (referrer, applicant, bonus status); sites (address, notes, contacts, type: school, hospital, office, and required eligibility flag); shifts; assignments (primary, backup A, backup B); availability (days, hours, can float); offers (ladder steps and results); attendance (confirmations, geofenced clock-ins); lessons; lesson_progress (watch time, unlock time, checks); external_certs (uploaded proof); eligibility (school and hospital flags set by the owner); recognition (badges, nominations); posts; supply_requests; leads and quotes; services (page content); assistant_settings (provider, encrypted key, spend cap); tool_policies (Auto/Ask/Never); audit_log (every action).

Stack

App: Next.js progressive web app, installable on a phone, English and Spanish through translation files.

Data and login: Postgres with row-level security (Supabase fits) and passkeys through a WebAuthn library.

Texting: an SMS provider such as Twilio. This is the one unavoidable running cost, a small per-text fee. US carriers require registering a business texting number first, which can take days, so start that early.

Jobs: a scheduler and queue for confirmations, timers and ladder steps.

Video: owner-made videos as unlisted YouTube embeds; vendor videos embedded or linked.

Assistant: a server-side gateway that holds the owner's key, exposes a short list of narrow tools, checks permissions in code and writes the audit log. The same tools can later be exposed through MCP (verify support per app first).

Geofencing: clock-in coordinates are stored only for the shift window, and workers are told so.

Phases

Phase 0, demo slice for the meeting. Clickable with sample data: the hiring card, the coverage board with a simulated call-out cascade at a sample school and a sample hospital, the assistant in owner mode on a test key, the training player with end-of-video unlock, the Spanish toggle on Rookie Run, a service page template and an About page shell. All sample data uses invented names and sites.

Phase 1, weeks 1 to 2. Real login with passkeys, real texting, live scheduling, real training content, owner console basics.

Phase 2. Recognition wall, Crew Hub, supply requests, site guides.

Phase 3. Assistant routines tuned to how he works; bench rules tuned from real call-out data.

